hypotheses.statement:
For every stage of <a href="#density:recursion" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="density:recursion">[density:recursion]</a>, the phase bandwidth of $W_j$ is at most $\ell_j$, its orbitwise mean is one, and $$\label{density:representing}
 \int_S p(\xi)W_j(\xi)\,d\sigma(\xi)=p(0)
 \quad\text{for every holomorphic polynomial }p.$$ Each individual correction has zero integral against every such polynomial, including the constant polynomial.

outputs.exact_statement:
There are absolute constants $C,c>0$, independent of $D_0\ge1$, such that $$\label{peaks:count}
 \frac{k}{D_0^2}\le N_k\le\frac{4k}{D_0^2}$$ and, for every $\xi\in S$ and $u\ge0$, $$\label{peaks:gaussian}
 \sum_{\substack{p\in\mathcal P_k\\\sqrt{k}d(\xi,p)\ge u}}
       |\langle\xi,p\rangle|^k\le Ce^{-cu^2}.$$ Consequently, $$\label{peaks:global}
 |P_k(z)|\le C|z|^k\quad(z\in\mathbb C^2),
 \qquad
 \int_S|P_k|\,d\sigma\le\frac{2N_k}{k+2}.$$

Fix $R_0>0$. If $D_0>\max\{1,2\sqrt{2R_0}\}$ and $k\ge\max\{D_0^2,2R_0\}$, the patches $\mathcal U_{k,p}$ are pairwise disjoint. On each patch, $$\label{peaks:patch-measure}
 d\sigma=\frac2k e^{-2y/k}\,dy\,
             \frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{d\gamma}{2\pi},$$ and $$\label{peaks:single-peak}
 |P_k(\xi)-e^{-y}e^{ik\theta}|
 \le C e^{-c(D_0-\sqrt{2R_0})^2}.$$ Outside their union, $$\label{peaks:off-patch}
 |P_k(\xi)|\le Ce^{-cR_0}.$$ The constants $C,c$ can be chosen independently of $R_0,D_0,k$.

Fix $1<a<2$ and put $\alpha=\log a$. One can choose $0<s_1<1$, smooth real functions $f,b$ on $[0,\infty)$, and $R_0>0$ such that $$\label{peaks:profile-negativity}
 \alpha^2-2s_1(\cosh\alpha-1)<0,$$ $$\label{peaks:profile-identities}
 \|f\|_\infty<1,\quad f=-s_1\ \text{on }[0,\alpha],\quad
 \int_0^\infty e^{-y}f(y)\,dy=0,\quad
 b'-b=f,\quad b(0)=0.$$ Both functions vanish on a neighborhood of $[R_0,\infty)$. Moreover, $R_0$ can be chosen so that $|aP_k|\le1/2$ off the patches whenever the hypotheses of Lemma <a href="#peaks:patches" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="peaks:patches">7</a> hold.

For every stage of <a href="#density:recursion" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="density:recursion">[density:recursion]</a>, the phase bandwidth of $W_j$ is at most $\ell_j$, its orbitwise mean is one, and $$\label{density:representing}
 \int_S p(\xi)W_j(\xi)\,d\sigma(\xi)=p(0)
 \quad\text{for every holomorphic polynomial }p.$$ Each individual correction has zero integral against every such polynomial, including the constant polynomial.

Let $k=k_j=Q^j$, where $Q$ satisfies the hypotheses of Theorem <a href="#density:main" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="density:main">10</a>. For $0\le r\le1$, $$\label{tests:averaging-identity}
 \int_S U_k(r\xi)W_j(\xi)\,d\sigma
 =
 \int_S U_k(r\xi)\,d\sigma
 +\sum_p\int_{\mathcal U_{k,p}}
     U_k(r\xi)e^{2y/k}f(y)\cos(k\theta)\,d\sigma.$$

In the frame just described, define the horizontal Hermitian form $$D=(1+2x)h-qhG^{-1}h.$$ The full curvature tensor is $$\label{curv:tensor-identity}
 R=-\lambda S_I-qS_h-S_V
    -(S_{D+V}-S_D-S_V)+T_4+T_3,$$ where $T_j$ has exactly $j$ horizontal indices. Its nonzero components, up to the Kähler symmetries and conjugation, are $$\begin{aligned}
 (T_4)_{i\bar j k\bar l}
   &=-x h_{i\bar j,k\bar l}
      +x^2G^{p\bar e}h_{i\bar e,k}h_{p\bar j,\bar l},
       \label{curv:four-horizontal-error}\\
 (T_3)_{i\bar j k\bar0}
   &=\sqrt q\bigl(-h_{i\bar j,k}
           +xG^{p\bar e}h_{i\bar e,k}h_{p\bar j}\bigr).
       \label{curv:three-horizontal-error}
\end{aligned}$$ Measured by the Euclidean component norms in this frame, uniformly for $\lambda\ge1$, $$\label{curv:component-errors}
 \|T_4\|\le C_4x,\qquad \|T_3\|\le C_3\sqrt q.$$ If $\lambda$ is at least the uniform upper bound for the eigenvalues of $h$ at centered-chart origins, then $$\label{curv:D-bounds}
 (1+x)h\le D\le(1+2x)h.$$

For the metric convention $g=2\operatorname{Re}\widehat g$ and the curvature convention <a href="#curv:coordinate-formula" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="curv:coordinate-formula">[curv:coordinate-formula]</a>, $$\label{curv:sectional}
 K_g(\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb R}\{U_1,U_2\})
       =\frac{\mathcal H_R}{2a_{\widehat g}}.$$ Define the matrix $$\label{curv:xi-definition}
 \Xi^{a\bar b}=u_1^a\overline{u_2^b}
                   -u_2^a\overline{u_1^b}.$$ For every tensor $T$ with the Kähler symmetries and Hermitian conjugation symmetry, $$\label{curv:xi-contraction}
 \mathcal H_T=-\frac12
 T_{a\bar b c\bar d}\Xi^{a\bar b}\Xi^{c\bar d}.$$ For every Hermitian form $P$, $$\label{curv:S-contraction}
 \mathcal H_{S_P}=a_P+3b_P^2.$$

For every real linearly independent tangent pair, $$\label{curv:contracted-errors}
 |\mathcal H_{T_4}|\le Cx a_I,\qquad
 |\mathcal H_{T_3}|\le C\sqrt q\,\sqrt{a_I m_I}.$$ More explicitly, the three-horizontal error satisfies $$\label{curv:mixed-error}
 |\mathcal H_{T_3}|
   \le C\sqrt q\,\|\Xi_{HH}\|\,
                         \|\Xi_{\mathrm{mix}}\|.$$
